## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design streaming algorithms with bounded memory while computing exact results. It captures a common real-world problem: maintaining aggregate statistics over a sliding or growing dataset without storing all historical values.

## Key Concepts

- **Streaming data structures:** Using heaps to maintain top-K elements efficiently
- **Running sum:** Incremental updates avoid recomputing the sum after each batch
- **Time complexity:** O(log K) per element; batch processing takes O(B log K)
- **Memory usage:** O(K) vs O(N) for the exact method that stores all past values

## Code Example

```javascript
function topKSumStream(valueStream, K) {
  const heap = new MinHeap();
  let sum = 0;

  for (const batch of valueStream) {
    for (const v of batch) {
      if (heap.size() < K) {
        heap.push(v);
        sum += v;
      } else if (heap.size() > 0 && v > heap.peek()) {
        sum += v - heap.pop();
        heap.push(v);
      }
    }
    console.log("Top-K sum:", sum);
  }
}
```

## Asymptotic Analysis

| Metric | Our Solution | Exact Method |
|--------|--------------|--------------|
| Per-element update | O(log K) | O(1) |
| Batch time (size B) | O(B log K) | O(B) |
| Memory | O(K) | O(N) |

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design streaming top-k algorithms within a sliding window using compact probabilistic data structures and articulate clear trade-offs between accuracy, space, and time.

## Key Concepts

- **Sliding window processing**: Maintaining state only over the most recent W elements
- **Space-Saving sketch**: A fixed-memory algorithm that provides approximate frequency counts
- **Top-k aggregation**: Identifying the k most frequent items in a stream
- **Approximation guarantees**: Bounding error in frequency estimates
- **Time/space complexity**: Analyzing per-operation and batch performance

## Code Example

```javascript
class SlidingTopK {
  constructor(k, W) {
    this.k = k;
    this.W = W;
    this.counters = new Map(); // item -> count
    this.window = []; // queue of last W items
  }

  add(x) {
    if (this.counters.has(x)) {
      this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x) + 1);
    } else if (this.counters.size < this.k) {
      this.counters.set(x, 1);
    } else {
      const minEntry = this.findMinCounter();
      this.counters.delete(minEntry.key);
      this.counters.set(x, minEntry.value + 1);
    }
    this.window.push(x);
    if (this.window.length > this.W) {
      this.expire(this.window.shift());
    }
  }

  expire(x) {
    if (this.counters.has(x)) {
      const newCount = this.counters.get(x) - 1;
      if (newCount > 0) {
        this.counters.set(x, newCount);
      } else {
        this.counters.delete(x);
      }
    }
  }

  findMinCounter() {
    let minEntry = { key: null, value: Infinity };
    for (const [key, value] of this.counters) {
      if (value < minEntry.value) {
        minEntry = { key, value };
      }
    }
    return minEntry;
  }

  topK() {
    return [...this.counters.entries()]
      .sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])
      .slice(0, this.k);
  }
}
```

